&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;c-message_kit__blocks c-message_kit__blocks--rich_text&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;c-message__message_blocks c-message__message_blocks--rich_text&quot; data-qa=&quot;message-text&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;p-block_kit_renderer&quot; data-qa=&quot;block-kit-renderer&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;p-block_kit_renderer__block_wrapper p-block_kit_renderer__block_wrapper--first&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;p-rich_text_block&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;p-rich_text_section&quot;&gt;Reddit is a community of communities. It’s built on shared interests, passion, and trust, and is home to the most open and authentic conversations on the internet. Every day, Reddit users submit, vote, and comment on the topics they care most about. With 100,000+ active communities and approximately 130 million daily active unique visitors, Reddit is one of the internet’s largest sources of information. For more information, visit &lt;a class=&quot;c-link&quot; href=&quot;http://www.redditinc.com/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; data-stringify-link=&quot;http://redditinc.com&quot; data-sk=&quot;tooltip_parent&quot;&gt;www.redditinc.com&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;Working as a Senior Growth Manager supporting Reddit’s International Community team, you will develop and execute initiatives that strengthen Reddit’s user and community ecosystems in the US and across international markets.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;This position is open to candidates based in the UK or the US - East Coast.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is not a marketing role. You will identify high-impact growth opportunities, design and execute experiments, and develop successful interventions into repeatable models that can be applied across markets. Your work may include building and scaling communities, increasing the supply of relevant content and contributions, reaching underserved audiences, and strengthening Reddit’s user experience.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The role combines growth strategy, hands-on experimentation, data analysis, and cross-functional influence. You will work closely with Product, Data Science, Marketing, and Community teams while maintaining the autonomy and entrepreneurial mindset required to scale successful initiatives to other markets.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;User &amp;amp; Community Growth Strategies: &lt;/strong&gt;Establish and execute comprehensive strategies to grow the user base and nurture communities.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Growth Experimentation:&lt;/strong&gt; Design and execute growth experiments aimed at addressing gaps in content supply, community density, contribution, discovery, engagement, and user growth. Apply a creative, entrepreneurial approach by testing ideas quickly, learning from results, and iterating accordingly.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Scaling and Repeatability:&lt;/strong&gt; Translate successful experiments into repeatable playbooks, processes, and recommendations that can be applied across markets. Determine which elements can scale broadly, which require local adaptation, and what operational or product support is needed to unlock broader impact.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Data &amp;amp; Performance Analytics: &lt;/strong&gt;Monitor key growth and ecosystem indicators, including DAU, contribution, content supply, community health, and retention. Analyze performance trends, identify risks and opportunities, and establish clear measurement frameworks for experiments and scaled programs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Cross-functional Collaboration: &lt;/strong&gt;Partner with various internal teams to provide insights, shape priorities, and scale growth initiatives. Build compelling evidence through experimentation to influence cross-functional investment and product development.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required Qualifications:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree or equivalent practical experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;7+ years of experience in user growth, product operations, or market expansion, with a demonstrated track record of executing growth initiatives at scale.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong entrepreneurial instincts, hands-on execution skills, and the ability to make progress independently in ambiguous or resource-constrained environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Data-driven and analytical mindset, with proficiency in Excel modeling, working knowledge of SQL, and experience creating scalable processes and automations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong systems thinking, with the ability to distinguish between market-specific problems and growth opportunities that can be addressed through repeatable approaches.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptional communication and stakeholder-management skills, with the ability to collaborate effectively and align cross-functional stakeholders across global teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Results-oriented mindset, strong attention to detail, and a bias toward execution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort balancing a portfolio of opportunities across the US and international markets and prioritizing based on potential impact, feasibility, and strategic relevance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;In select roles and locations, the interviews will be recorded, transcribed and summarized by artificial intelligence (AI). You will have the opportunity to opt out of recording, transcription and summarization prior to any scheduled interviews.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;During the interview, we will collect the following categories of personal information: Identifiers, Professional and Employment-Related Information, Sensory Information (audio/video recording), and any other categories of personal information you choose to share with us. We will use this information to evaluate your application for employment or an independent contractor role, as applicable.&amp;nbsp; We will not sell your personal information or disclose it to any third party for their marketing purposes.&amp;nbsp; We will delete any recording of your interview promptly after making a hiring decision.&amp;nbsp; For more information about how we will handle your personal information, including our retention of it, please refer to our &lt;a href=&quot;https://redditinc.com/policies/candidate-privacy-policy&quot;&gt;Candidate Privacy Policy for Potential Employees and Contractors&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Reddit is proud to be an equal opportunity employer, and is committed to building a workforce representative of the diverse communities we serve.&amp;nbsp; Reddit is committed to providing reasonable accommodations for qualified individuals with disabilities and disabled veterans in our job application procedures. If, due to a disability, you need an accommodation during the interview process, please let your recruiter know.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Director of Data (m/f/d)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Reporting to the CTO, you will own the data strategy and execution for Moonfare at a pivotal moment in our growth. We are building the infrastructure and intelligence layer that will power how we serve investors, operate as a business, and scale into new markets, and data is the foundation everything else depends on. You will inherit a capable team and a real mandate: to bring it together, raise the bar, and build a data function that is fit for where Moonfare is going, not just where it has been. The role demands someone who can hold the strategic vision and get into the technical detail, knowing when to lead from the front and when to elevate the people around them. In return, you get a rare scope, shaping how a fast-growing private equity platform thinks about, structures, and activates its data from the ground up.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role sits at the intersection of Engineering, Product, and the wider business, leading our combined Data Engineering and Analytics function. The team is 6 people across pipelines, analytics, and architecture who will come together under your leadership into one cohesive function with a shared mission. The team&#39;s work underpins how Moonfare makes decisions, serves its investors, and builds towards an AI-driven operating model, making this one of the highest-leverage functions in the business.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You will:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define and execute the data strategy for Moonfare, building the platforms, pipelines, and governance that give the business a reliable, scalable, and intelligent data foundation to grow on.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bring 6 people across data engineering, analytics, and architecture into one cohesive team, setting the operating model, rituals, and standards that make the function more than the sum of its parts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Architect and build the infrastructure that sources, structures, and serves data across investment, investor relations, operations, and compliance use cases.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner closely with Engineering and Product to make data the substrate that our AI and agentic capabilities are built on, and with the business to enable self-serve reporting and operational intelligence.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Stay deep in the technical detail across architecture reviews, design decisions, and pipeline trade-offs, while also representing data credibly to executive stakeholders and the Board.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Embed compliance and regulatory thinking into every layer of the platform, recognising the demands of operating in a regulated financial services environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The next Moonfarian:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You bring deep, hands-on expertise across data engineering, AI, architecture, and pipelines. You lead the strategy and get into the weeds with your team on the hardest technical problems, contributing directly rather than just directing from a distance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You&#39;ve built or significantly evolved a modern data platform in a regulated financial services environment, and you understand what compliance, auditability, and data quality actually demand at the architecture level.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have a strong, opinionated point of view on what modern AI and agentic systems need from a data function, and you&#39;ve put that thinking into practice in real products and platforms, not just on slides.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You&#39;re an experienced people leader who has unified or scaled a multi-disciplinary data team, and can bring engineers, analysts, and architects together around a shared mission while knowing when to roll up your sleeves alongside them.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You thrive in pressured, high-ambiguity scale-up environments and are energised by carrying both the strategic load and a meaningful share of the technical work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You&#39;re a credible partner to executives and cross-functional stakeholders, able to translate between business outcomes and technical reality.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We can only accept applications from those eligible to live and work in London. This is a hybrid role with office attendance required 4 days/week.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Please note that we do not accept applications sent by email. You should submit your application directly through our careers website.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Invest in Yourself:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Ownership and Impact: &lt;/strong&gt;You are empowered to bring ideas, make decisions, and see your work directly contribute to Moonfare&#39;s success.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Transparent Environment: &lt;/strong&gt;We believe in open communication. You will receive regular updates on company strategy, performance against our KPIs, and key business decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Personal Growth: &lt;/strong&gt;We support your development with an individual growth budget of £1,500 or 2% of your base salary (whichever is higher).&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Invest in Your Future: &lt;/strong&gt;We support your long-term financial goals with a workplace pension via SmartPension, where Moonfare contributes 3% and combined employer and employee contributions reach at least 8%.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Relax and Recharge: &lt;/strong&gt;You start with 25 vacation days and you&#39;ll receive one additional day for each year of tenure, up to a maximum of 30 days. Moonfare gifts two days during our annual end of year company shutdown.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Daily Lunch: &lt;/strong&gt;Enjoy a £12 daily lunch allowance via Deliveroo on the days you&#39;re in the London office, delivered or ready to pick up nearby.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Fitness and Wellbeing: &lt;/strong&gt;Stay active with a subsidised FitnessFirst membership, with £30 covered by Moonfare each month and no joining fee, plus a monthly guest pass and company wellness events.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Health Cover:&lt;/strong&gt; Look after your health with private medical and dental cover through Bupa, including Select Complete Healthcare across 600 partner facilities and Dental Plan Level 2, with dependants covered up to age 24.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Cycle to Work:&lt;/strong&gt; Ride in tax-efficiently through our salary-sacrifice scheme via Forest, available for an eBike or eMoped.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A Culture of Excellence:&lt;/strong&gt; Join a team of ambitious, smart, and committed professionals who are passionate about revolutionising private market investing.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Performance Reward: &lt;/strong&gt;As a performance-first company, we reward strong performance twice a year, so your impact translates directly into how your pay grows — through potential base salary increases and/or bonuses.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our Values:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our clients come first, Moonfare comes second, and we prioritise ourselves third - Client-Centric Focus. &lt;/strong&gt;Putting clients first means creating value for them is essential. Placing Moonfare second signifies that our individual professional future at Moonfare depends on the company&#39;s commercial success. Prioritising ourselves third reflects our humility in putting clients and Moonfare before personal interests.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We pursue excellence and honor our promises - Commitment to Excellence. &lt;/strong&gt;We hold ourselves to the highest standards, taking responsibility for our failures, and celebrating our successes. We commit to deadlines and stick to them and we learn from our mistakes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We are here to win and to celebrate our collective achievements - Win together. &lt;/strong&gt;We are mission-focused and think and act like owners. We exemplify the attitude we expect and each of us commits to do what it takes to succeed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We foster personal growth but each of us earns our place as a Moonfarian through merit - Growth and Merit. &lt;/strong&gt;We hire, retain, and develop exceptional people and invest in empowering them to excel. We must all earn our place at the table every day.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We understand the important role that diversity plays in our success. Different backgrounds, experiences and ideas push us further and raise the bar. We’re committed to developing an inclusive and safe culture where everyone&amp;nbsp; — regardless of colour, race, religion, sex, origin, sexuality, disability, marital status, citizenship or gender identity — knows that they are an integral part of the team and can bring their full potential to their work.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;We’re in an unbelievably exciting area of tech and are fundamentally reshaping the data storage industry. Here, you lead with innovative thinking, grow along with us, and join the smartest team in the industry.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This type of work—work that changes the world—is what the tech industry was founded on. So, if you&#39;re ready to seize the endless opportunities and leave your mark, come join us.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;THE ROLE&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Senior Lead&amp;nbsp; Product Services Engineer role is critical to building the foundation of scalable services at Everpure. You will define how Product capabilities are operationalised, ensuring that product adoption is supported by consistent, high-quality service frameworks. The role is responsible for engineering and operationalising repeatable platform services that support the lifecycle of Everpure products.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Role is expected to demonstrate the appropriate level of technical and thought leadership and internal cross-functional influence, as well as to devise new quality methods, content and innovations to accelerate enablement and influence quality.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Leading another Platform Services Engineer, the role is responsible for driving and ensuring completion of all delivery readiness requirements, as well as the automation, and standardisation of product-attached services, ensuring they can be deployed consistently, efficiently, and at global scale. Working closely with Product Engineering, Portfolio, and Delivery teams, the role translates product capabilities into scalable service offerings that improve operational efficiency and accelerate customer adoption.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;WHAT YOU&#39;LL DO&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Strategy:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help define Platform services scope&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define a robust Delivery Readiness Framework for successful deployment (integrating with existing workflows)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define service readiness criteria, operational documentation, and enablement assets before global release.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define &amp;amp; Establish service standards, quality measures, SLAs, and operational best practices.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure product services are aligned to product releases and engineering roadmaps.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Delivery Operational Readiness:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as the intersection between Product Engineering &amp;amp; Advanced Services ensuring every product service is operationally ready prior to release (Field Testing / QA)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Product Engineering to operationalise new platform capabilities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work closely with Engineering / Product Team on Tech Documentation ( version control / management)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify Enablement requirements (Partners, CDP, ASP)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ongoing Software Release impact assessment and notifications&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Services Engineering Lab Management strategy / Overview&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Innovation (Continuous Improvement &amp;amp; Automation)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Adopt a Six Sigma type approach to continuous improvement / efficiencies in workflows and technology through automation, simplification, and standardisation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead with an AI innovation mindset - Develop service automation, tooling, runbooks, and operational procedures to improve consistency and quality and&amp;nbsp; constantly enhance scalable service frameworks that improve operational efficiency &amp;amp; accelerate customer adoption.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Leadership&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead Platform Services Engineer(s)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Program Management approach /&amp;nbsp; governance&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Close collaboration with Stakeholders / Leadership Teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as Technical SME for wider Implementation Center of Excellence Team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;WHAT YOU BRING&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong experience in Product engineering, infrastructure, or cloud environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understanding of product lifecycle and operational service design&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building automation and standardised operational processes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with enterprise Products (storage, cloud, virtualization, networking)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with scripting or automation tools (e.g. Terraform, Python, CI/CD pipelines)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to design scalable, repeatable service models rather than one-off solutions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong collaboration skills across architecture, product, and engineering teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Attention to detail and focus on operational excellence&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong Documentation and asset management (version control) skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge / experience&amp;nbsp; of Continuous Improvement Methodologies (ie Six Sigma) preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;#LI-Remote&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;WHAT YOU CAN EXPECT FROM US:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Innovation&lt;/strong&gt;: We celebrate those who think critically, like a challenge, and aspire to be trailblazers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Growth&lt;/strong&gt;: We give you the space and support to grow along with us and to contribute to something meaningful. We have been named Fortune&#39;s Best Workplaces in Technology™, Fortune&#39;s Best Workplaces in the Bay Area™, and certified as a Great Place to Work®!&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Team&lt;/strong&gt;: We build each other up and set aside ego for the greater good.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;And because we understand the value of bringing your full and best self to work, we offer a variety of perks to manage a healthy balance, including flexible time off, wellness resources, and company-sponsored team events. Check out &lt;a href=&quot;http://purebenefits.com&quot;&gt;purebenefits.com&lt;/a&gt; for more information.&lt;/p&gt;
