&lt;p&gt;The CRM Account Director is responsible for building and growing strategic client relationships while ensuring clients realise measurable value from their CRM investment. Acting as a trusted advisor, they work closely with senior client stakeholders to shape CRM strategy, drive adoption, identify growth opportunities and ensure successful delivery across marketing, technology and data initiatives.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;The role combines commercial account leadership with strategic CRM consulting, partnering with internal cross-functional teams to deliver outstanding client outcomes and long-term customer success.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Job Description&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Strategic Client Leadership&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build trusted relationships with senior client stakeholders, including CRM Directors, Marketing Directors, Digital Directors and C-suite executives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop a deep understanding of each client&#39;s business objectives, commercial priorities and CRM maturity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead strategic account planning to ensure CRM programmes align with wider business goals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as the executive point of contact for strategic accounts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;CRM Strategy&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advise clients on CRM best practice across customer acquisition, onboarding, engagement, retention, loyalty and reactivation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help clients define CRM roadmaps and transformation strategies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Recommend opportunities to improve customer journeys through personalisation, automation, AI and first-party data.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translate business objectives into measurable CRM programmes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Customer Success&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own overall client health, satisfaction and long-term success.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead Quarterly Business Reviews (QBRs) and Executive Business Reviews.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor adoption, utilisation and business outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure clients achieve measurable ROI against agreed success metrics.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proactively identify risks and drive mitigation plans.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Commercial Growth&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify opportunities to expand client relationships through additional products and services.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop account growth plans aligned to client priorities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead commercial conversations around renewals, upsell and cross-sell opportunities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work closely with Sales to execute account expansion strategies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Project &amp;amp; Delivery Oversight&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Delivery, Product, Engineering and Solution Consulting teams to ensure successful implementation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure projects remain aligned with agreed business outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Escalate and resolve delivery risks where required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain executive visibility throughout complex programmes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Data &amp;amp; Insights&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use customer data and campaign performance to identify optimisation opportunities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Present strategic recommendations based on business insights.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help clients maximise value product offerings.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive a culture of continuous optimisation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Executive Communication&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Present confidently to executive stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Facilitate strategic workshops.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Influence senior decision makers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Produce clear executive-level recommendations and business cases.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
